# Budders: a kind that only buds, for watching genes pass from parent to child
# (scenarios/tests/genes_inherit and genes_drift). A budder buds into a free
# neighbouring cell while fewer than twelve budders stand within its `reach`, and
# dies of age after a day, so a world of them turns over a generation about
# every day. `reach` is a gene: each budder has its own, a child starts with
# its parent's, and a scenario's `mutation` line makes it drift.

kind budder {
  glyph "b"
  color "#9fd36b"
  cadence 256
  sight 10
  gene reach = 5 from 1 to 10     # how far it looks for crowding
  when age > 1d => die
  when count budder within reach < 12 and nearest free within 1 as c => spawn budder at c
}
